    <!-- Practice, Bio & CV -->
    <section class="section" id="about">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-header">
          <div>
            <div class="section-kicker mono">Biography &amp; Approach</div>
            <h2 class="section-title">Slow Observation</h2>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="about-grid">
          <div class="portrait-card">
            <div class="portrait-frame">
              <img id="studioPortraitImg" alt="Monochrome light study from Clara Moreau's studio" />
            </div>
            <div class="mono" style="color: var(--ink-muted); display: flex; justify-content: space-between;">
              <span>Studio 4B, Lisbon</span>
              <span>Ilford Delta 100 · 80mm</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div>
            <p class="about-lead">
              “A photograph is less about capturing what stands before the lens, and more about listening to how light alters a room over an hour.”
            </p>

            <div class="about-body">
              <p>
                Born in Lyon and trained in architectural history before turning full-time to photography, my work sits at the intersection of spatial geometry and human quietude. Whether documenting a brutalist pavilion at dawn or a rain-washed Parisian boulevard after midnight, I favor unhurried pacing and natural light.
              </p>
              <p>
                Most commissions are photographed on medium-format 120 film alongside digital capture for rapid editorial turnaround. Every project is color-graded in-house to preserve delicate shadow detail and tactile tonal transitions.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="services-grid">
              <div class="service-item">
                <h4>Editorial &amp; Documentary</h4>
                <p>Long-form visual essays, travel features, and cultural profiles for print journals and monographs.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="service-item">
                <h4>Architecture &amp; Interiors</h4>
                <p>Atmosphere-driven documentation for architectural studios, boutique hotels, and design residences.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="service-item">
                <h4>Brand Campaigns</h4>
                <p>Quiet, narrative-led lookbooks and still-life direction for fashion, ceramic, and fragrance houses.</p>
              </div>
